projection always exact"},{"id":"K5_forward_order","requirement":"Forward and side-effect order is NOT judged, within or across slaves.","source":"none public","assumptions":[],"support_status":"excluded; listed in every scoped_pass"},{"id":"K6_response_order","requirement":"A master response in row c retires that master's oldest live entry from rows < c; an ACK or non-HR ERR with no such entry kills the hypothesis. An ERR under HR(m,c) (held, or acceptance edge after identical held row) branches: A ordinary retirement; B retire nothing (possible_starvation_err); in case (ii) B2 moves the row-c entry to the canceled pool tagged starvation_attributed. Association-free bound: ACKs + non-HR ERRs in the current CYC <= acceptances in earlier rows of that CYC; HR ERRs counted separately. Repeated HR ERRs during one held request are not judged and stay unknown.","source":"README 188-196; WB B4 3.1.3.2; wbxbar.v header 37-39","assumptions":["Inferred clause"],"support_status":"implemented; inferred; suspended on exhaustion except count bound"},{"id":"K7_ack_basis_read_data","requirement":"A master ACK requires the retired entry to be bound to a slave ACK in a row <= c in the same hypothesis; for reads the full 32-bit o_mdata equals that slave ACK's i_sdata slice.","source":"WB B4 obs 3.10; 3.1.3.2; README","assumptions":["Same-row slave-to-master path allowed"],"support_status":"implemented; suspended on exhaustion"},{"id":"K8_errors","requirement":"ACK retiring an unmapped or slave-ERRed entry kills the hypothesis; ERR retiring them is consistent; ERR retiring a mapped entry without slave ERR is tagged unexplained_mapped_err (unknown). No eventual-ERR or deadline claim.","source":"WB B4 perm 3.20, rule 3.45; crossbar article; wbxbar.v header 32-39","assumptions":[],"support_status":"implemented; unknown cases unresolved; suspended on exhaustion"},{"id":"K9_cancellation_orphans","requirement":"On a row with pre i_mcyc[m]=0, unforwarded live entries become distinct canceled-pool members tagged (master, master_epoch, reset_epoch, accept_row); forwarded ones become orphans whose slave responses bind positionally and never reach a master. Consuming a pool member (including same-row as the drop) is tagged post_abort_forward. Canceled identities persist until reset.","source":"WB B4 3.1.2, rule 3.30; crossbar article (supplementary)","assumptions":["No C1 certificate, so no mid-epoch release"],"support_status":"implemented; residual forwards unresolved"},{"id":"K10_dut_master_handshake","requirement":"A DUT-stalled slave request must persist with identical identity projection or o_scyc drops; o_sstb without o_scyc and o_mack&o_merr are violations; undefined DUT control outputs are violations.","source":"WB B4 3.1.3.2, rules 3.25, 3.45","assumptions":[],"support_status":"implemented; association-free"},{"id":"K11_env","requirement":"Master hold change/withdrawal under stall with CYC high, slave ACK&ERR together, slave response with empty FIFO or while o_scyc is low, undefined inputs, malformed rows and missing initial reset are environment violations (input_or_scope_invalid). Slave CYC withdrawal marks FIFO forwards slave_canceled. Processing stops at the first env row e.","source":"Packet environment_contract; WB 3.30, 3.45","assumptions":["Assumption clause"],"support_status":"implemented"},{"id":"K12_batch_end","requirement":"Live non-slave-canceled entries unretired at trace end in any surviving history yield pending_at_batch_end (unresolved), never a liveness failure; slave_canceled live entries, pool members and orphans are non-obligations (counted only).","source":"Packet requested obligations","assumptions":[],"support_status":"implemented; reporting"},{"id":"K13_response_without_cyc","requirement":"o_mack/o_merr with pre i_mcyc low in rows c-1 and c is a DUT violation; if i_mcyc fell exactly in row c it is unresolved same_edge_response_after_abort and never retired.","source":"WB B4 3.1.2, rule 3.30 (inferred reading)","assumptions":["First trace row has no c-1 and is not judged"],"support_status":"implemented; inferred"},{"id":"LIMITS","requirement":"Default MAX_HYP=4096, MAX_LIVE_PER_MASTER=64, MAX_CANCELED_POOL=256; optional limits dict (development selftests only) validated as positive ints. On exhaustion: no pruning, unresolved_on_limit with sizes, association clauses suspended for all masters until reset, suspended rows/fraction reported.","source":"Reviewed resource_limits","assumptions":[],"support_status":"implemented"},{"id":"VERDICT","requirement":"DUT violations wholly before e stay dut_violation; pin-only DUT checks at row e stay; association-dependent DUT candidates at row e become mixed_same_edge unresolved; otherwise input_or_scope_invalid if e exists, else violation > unresolved > scoped_pass. Prefix status reported. scoped_pass excludes K5 and C1-C4 and means not refuted by the reference.","source":"Reviewed verdict_semantics","assumptions":[],"support_status":"implemented"},{"id":"FORMAL_F1_F8","requirement":"Formal obligations F1-F8 and characterization C1-C4.","source":"Reviewed formal_obligations","assumptions":[],"support_status":"unproved targets; not implemented"}],"contract_markdown":"# WBXBAR exact-history reference checker (candidate)

Scope: public pins of WBXBAR rev 2e8d3bc2, NM=2, NS=2, AW=8, DW=32, slave0 = (addr&0xf0)==0x00, slave1 = (addr&0xf0)==0x10. Rows are pre/post samples; only pre defines transfers, post is used for K1 reset outputs. Candidate only: independent controls, code review, freeze and replay are required before any B/C.

## Model
Exact explicit hypothesis set H per reset epoch; no quotient, partition, deduplication or pruning. Each hypothesis holds per-master FIFOs of live entries (identity, accept_row, master_epoch, reset_epoch, state unforwarded/forwarded/slave_acked/slave_erred/slave_canceled), a canceled pool of distinct members, orphans, per-slave forward FIFOs and a tag list. Row order: reset; CYC drop; master acceptances; slave CYC withdrawal; slave responses (bind to forwards from rows < c); slave acceptances (branch over every identity-equal candidate); master responses (K13, then K6/K7/K8 against entries from rows < c); association-free checks.

## Verdicts
scoped_pass, dut_violation, input_or_scope_invalid, unresolved only. Per-clause statuses are in counts.property_status (violated, suspended, unresolved, checked_not_refuted, prefix_checked_not_refuted, excluded_not_judged). scoped_pass means not refuted by the reference on this trace; it excludes K5 forward order and unproved characterization C1-C4, and is not proof of hidden ownership. Ownership per epoch is unique_by_elimination or indistinguishable(k) in counts.pending_alternatives.

Time-bounded precedence: e = first row with an environment violation; processing stops there. DUT violations before e stay final. At row e, pin-only DUT checks (K1, K2 slave payload, K3, K10, K13, rule 3.45) stay dut_violation; association-dependent candidates (empty H, K4/K6 count projections) become mixed_same_edge(dut_candidate, env), unresolved, with a note that no public ordering exists. counts.prefix_status gives prefix_scoped_pass / prefix_unresolved / prefix_dut_violation for rows < e.

## Unknown tags
post_abort_forward, unexplained_mapped_err, same_edge_response_after_abort, possible_starvation_err, starvation_attributed; any unclassified tag defaults to unknown. Tags carried by any surviving history are flushed to cumulative unresolved records at reset and batch end; reset never erases cumulative uncertainty.

Repeated HR ERRs during one held request are absorbed by branch B and are not judged; they stay unknown.

## Resource limits
Defaults MAX_HYP=4096, MAX_LIVE_PER_MASTER=64, MAX_CANCELED_POOL=256. The limits argument is for development selftests only and is validated; frozen callers pass rows only. On exhaustion: unresolved_on_limit(row, sizes), association clauses (K4 per-candidate, K6, K7, K8 attribution, K9 tags, K12) suspended for all masters until reset; still checked: K1, K2, K3, K10, K11, K13, rule 3.45, K4 per-identity count projection, per-slave response count, per-CYC ACK+non-HR-ERR bound. Counters are arbitrary-precision Python ints. counts.checked_scope reports suspended rows, fraction, exhaustion rows/sizes and effective checked rows.

## Declared exclusions
K5 order; C1-C4; liveness/latency/deadlines; payload while STB low, read-data lanes on requests, SEL-disabled lanes; write ACK data; reset-row master responses beyond K13/3.45; rule 3.05 sub-row reset length; formal F1-F8 unproved.

## Implementation decisions and blockers (not settled by the reviewed contract)
- B2 when the row-c entry was already forwarded in the same row: treated as orphan with post_abort_forward + starvation_attributed tags (blocker: contract silent).
- Undefined i_sdata on a slave ACK is an env violation only if at least one history binds it to a live read (blocker: hypothesis-dependent env classification).
- Simultaneous o_mack&o_merr: rule 3.45 violation, response not attributed.
- K13 is not judged on the first trace row (no c-1).
- The K6 count bound uses acceptances from earlier rows of the current CYC (consistent with K6 retiring only rows < c).
- Master STB without CYC is not an acceptance and is not separately flagged.
- slave_canceled live entries at batch end are counted (non-obligation), not pending.
- A row with undefined DUT control output is a DUT violation and stops judgment (unjudgeable_row).
- Mixed same-edge pin-only vs association-dependent split as described above.
- Events list is always empty; no recovery event or ownership proof is invented.
- Identical histories are not merged, so exhaustion may occur earlier than with a quotient; this is reported, never pruned.
